cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Percolation after Anthropic: Lean 4 proofs of the Kozma-Nitzan connection inequalities and of site percolation at criticality"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib development of the Kozma-Nitzan connection inequalities for
  Bernoulli percolation (Conjectures 1-4 and 6, affirmative answers to Questions 5, 7 and 9, and a
  counterexample to the every-minimizer reading of Question 8), their extension to independent
  hyperedges, and the theorem that nearest-neighbour Bernoulli site percolation on Z^d, d >= 3,
  has no infinite open cluster at its critical parameter. It builds on the bond-percolation proof
  of Anthropic, a pinned git dependency. The library contains no sorry and no custom axiom; the
  Mathlib-only comparator challenge for the site theorem contains one intentional statement-level
  sorry whose completed solution is checked separately.
type: software
authors:
